{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790529881,"nonce":"FK/KZuYLwfZ0ABgrHICWhYol3dw=","title":"Show named CSS color swatches in the GIC editor","message":"## What to build\n\nShow a small Monaco color swatch beside recognized CSS named-color literals in GIC color arguments (`background`, `fill`, and `stroke`). The editor already enables `colorDecorators`, but GIC has no registered color provider. Use the accepted names in `src/color-names.ts` as the source of truth.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A valid named color in a color-string argument displays a swatch matching the rendered color.\n- Unrelated strings, comments, and invalid color names do not display swatches.\n- Editing or replacing the literal updates or removes its swatch.\n- A browser acceptance test verifies visible swatches in the real Monaco editor.\n\nThis is separate from the existing named-color autocomplete feature (98354e4).","files":null}]}